-- title:
--   Coordinate power relations imply finiteness over the generated algebra
-- statement:
--   If a common positive weighted-homogeneous generating family for an ideal contains a positive power of each coordinate variable in that ideal, then the polynomial ring is finite as a module over the algebra generated by the family.
-- source:
--   openai/math Ampleness stack: WeightedIdealCurveBound implies eps-ample exceptional twist, hence Serre vanishing and eventual generation of I^n by weight ≤ n(rho+eps) sections.

